# The admin's ports, in Island Hop.
# Every port these tests add is named "HumanTest test port"; "Start with: no test ports"
# removes any that a failed run left behind (see e2e/states/no-test-ports.ts).

Test: Admin adds a port and deletes it again

  Start with: no test ports

  As admin:
    go to ports page
    click "Add Port"
    "Add New Port" dialog should be open
    type "HumanTest test port" in "Port Name"
    choose "America/Anguilla" for "Time Zone"
    click "Create Port"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/ports
    backend should reply 201 Created
    should see "Port created successfully"
    "Add New Port" dialog should be closed
    in "HumanTest test port" row, click "Open menu"
    click "Delete port"
    in "Delete Port" dialog, click "Delete"
    backend should receive DELETE /api/v1/ports/:id
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Port permanently deleted"


# The name field has no "required", so the page's own check is what stops it.
Test: The port form stops before sending when the name is empty

  As admin:
    go to ports page
    click "Add Port"
    choose "America/Anguilla" for "Time Zone"
    click "Create Port"
    should see "Port name is required"
    backend should not receive any request
    "Add New Port" dialog should be open


Test: The port form stops before sending when no time zone is chosen

  As admin:
    go to ports page
    click "Add Port"
    type "HumanTest test port" in "Port Name"
    click "Create Port"
    should see "Time zone is required"
    backend should not receive any request
    "Add New Port" dialog should be open
